  [dependencies] package.json:sharp  — Next.js's image optimiser loads sharp itself at runtime, by name, from the server bundle — there is no import of it in this repo and there must not be one. Removing it makes next/image fall back to the slow unoptimised path in production. Stale the day next/image is no longer used or Next bundles its own encoder
  [devDependencies] package.json:@tailwindcss/typography  — same shape one line further down: globals.css line 3 is `@plugin "@tailwindcss/typography"`, a Tailwind 4 CSS-first plugin registration with no JS import anywhere. Stale the day that @plugin line is removed
  [devDependencies] package.json:tailwindcss  — loaded by CSS, not by the module graph: globals.css line 1 is `@import "tailwindcss"`, resolved by @tailwindcss/postcss at build time. knip reads TypeScript imports and cannot see a CSS @import. Stale the day the project stops importing tailwind from CSS
  [binaries] package.json:feedbucket-widget  — not a binary. knip parses package.json script strings as shell, and `check:cycles` passes madge `--exclude "node_modules|\.next|feedbucket-widget"`; the `|` characters read as pipeline separators, so the last alternative of the regex is reported as a command being run. It is a directory name inside a regex. Stale the day that --exclude pattern changes shape
